{"kind":"request","text":"Builder: Complete browser task, progress, steering and review journey. Implementation work package 5 of the reviewed connected-story design (planning b5f1fb3f, exact Draft2 evidence209a5ec9, approvalfc77cf82 and adopted direction0f358e52). Source baseline e6e6782 and the active acts/MCP a199 composition are context, not approval; reconcile current reviewed main, relevant existing requests and ecbc722a runner changes before editing.\n\nScope and decisions:\nWire a real live browser entry and the existing four Room screens to the production Agent API, client and authoritative Room adapter. Main/a199 still select a mock at page entry; existing live-adapter code is a starting point, not delivered onboarding/agent integration. Add a task panel linked to room/lane and small-screen controls; a permanent extra chat screen, browser terminal/IDE/preview and harness marketplace are later work.\nConnect create/join/import, task goal/scope/agent identity/owner/budget, durable submit, claim, fork/compute/dependency preparation, watch, steering, attention, pause/resume/cancel, exact-head proposal review and landing/publication. Show accepted/queued/applied steering states and each operation's durable boundary. Agent questions and Room obligations need distinct responses. Show conversation activity beside Room lane/proposal/review/landing/log facts; prose saying 'done' cannot create an authoritative result.\nKeep separate conversation and Room cursors; reconnect from saved cursors or a complete snapshot. Offline/stale status retains the last confirmed watermark. Expose actionable waiting/failure/disconnection/unknown/reconciliation states and durable cleanup duties; reuse 8d249233 rather than inventing completion by timeout. Closing a tab does not pause/cancel. Cancel cannot undo completed effects. Review uses the person's own current key, exact head/diff/verdict scope/current or carried/stale evidence, and qualification; refresh on newer proposal/policy and preserve declared bindings. Request landing through the holder agent and separately show agent-finished, proposed, landed and published-through. Small-screen review must display head and scope before signing.\nApply the reconciled design decisions, not Draft1 wording: existing sessions are read-only; controls use signed resource/action-bound current owner/admin requests. Initially one new agent member and one DO/conversation/lane per task; no in-place owner reassignment. Last-active-owner-key revocation or owner removal stops new tools/broker writes/renewals; another active owner device keeps independent-agent work alive. Admins retain private export/settlement, and lost-key recovery restores only an active member, never a removed handle. Optional delegated agent mode is not required in initial runtime delivery; its key-bound grantor rules and conditional acceptance remain specified. Render repository/command output inert in the key-owning origin and expose only minimal activity to other Room readers.\nPrivate-read contract decision carried from independent revised-design review: initial raw owner/admin resources require a direct device read session, whose direct-key provenance and current role/resource are verified by the trusted Room boundary. authenticateRead returning an owner/admin member handle is insufficient. Deny delegation-issued read sessions raw resources by default; any separately scoped private-read capability is later explicit contract work. Sessions stay read-only, and controls remain separately signed.\n\nDependencies and order:\nRequired relevant reviewed decisions/deliveries: git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:13dfc613e8e3d9a1aed5f7492272fbf8c580d727, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:18815307e6c306d63766230ed7eb7ddbf94d1f21, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:a5d64b35e87c97560ff354578d9560bd1261aacb. Live reviewed portions of production Agent runtime and browser identity/onboarding; existing declared-client/UI stage5 functional work retained; explicit policy/bootstrap and cleanup read integration. Do not duplicate those requests or require completed unrelated stages before this package can develop. Highest implementation priority remains test-overhead ecbc722a, followed by acts and builder-identified Jam blockers; this request adds no first-Jam readiness gate. Report source/design discrepancies before weakening scope.\n\nAcceptance outcome:\nA fresh user completes one useful repository change entirely through browser controls, watches progress, answers attention, requests correction, signs a qualified review and follows real landing/log publication. Start on A, close it, continue watch/steer/review on authorized B. Include a lost input reply, reconnect, explicit pause/cancel and uncertain publication with different visible recovery actions. A deliberately false agent 'done' message changes no Room result. Unauthorized/revoked devices cannot watch private data or steer. Use one compact real browser journey and meaningful recovery/authorization witnesses. Show execution-ended-but-save-failed separately from durable completion and retain the previous checkpoint. Show explicit expired data and unresolved reconciliation; a successful new attempt must not hide the earlier unknown duty.\n\nValidation:\nKnown existing runners: npm run typecheck; npm test --workspace @generalbusiness/artroom-ui; npm run e2e --workspace @generalbusiness/artroom-ui. Use affected live-adapter/task files and one compact browser scenario plus meaningful recovery witnesses; final retained gate at exact delivered head. Reconcile the runner changes from ecbc722a before naming the exact filtered commands in your promise.\n\nDelivery: use an isolated request branch/worktree, record promise and exact source/probe evidence, publish every changed path at the exact delivered head, and obtain independent normal review before integration. Source code/protocol amendments are not authorized by the evidence-only design verdict alone. No numerical test inventory/per-guard sweep, no new first-Jam readiness gate. If a provider/storage/authority mechanism cannot meet the stated story, report a design discrepancy rather than silently reducing scope.","body":{"conditions":"A fresh user completes one useful repository change entirely through browser controls, watches progress, answers attention, requests correction, signs a qualified review and follows real landing/log publication. Start on A, close it, continue watch/steer/review on authorized B. Include a lost input reply, reconnect, explicit pause/cancel and uncertain publication with different visible recovery actions. A deliberately false agent 'done' message changes no Room result. Unauthorized/revoked devices cannot watch private data or steer. Use one compact real browser journey and meaningful recovery/authorization witnesses. Show execution-ended-but-save-failed separately from durable completion and retain the previous checkpoint. Show explicit expired data and unresolved reconciliation; a successful new attempt must not hide the earlier unknown duty. Required relevant reviewed decisions/deliveries: git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:13dfc613e8e3d9a1aed5f7492272fbf8c580d727, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:18815307e6c306d63766230ed7eb7ddbf94d1f21, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:a5d64b35e87c97560ff354578d9560bd1261aacb. Relevant contract decisions and exact implementation evidence independently reviewed; source artifacts integrated through normal landing. Preserve named lifecycle/authority/durability rules and existing owed work. Known existing runners: npm run typecheck; npm test --workspace @generalbusiness/artroom-ui; npm run e2e --workspace @generalbusiness/artroom-ui. Use affected live-adapter/task files and one compact browser scenario plus meaningful recovery witnesses; final retained gate at exact delivered head. Reconcile the runner changes from ecbc722a before naming the exact filtered commands in your promise.","dependencies":"Required relevant reviewed decisions/deliveries: git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:13dfc613e8e3d9a1aed5f7492272fbf8c580d727, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:18815307e6c306d63766230ed7eb7ddbf94d1f21, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:a5d64b35e87c97560ff354578d9560bd1261aacb. Live reviewed portions of production Agent runtime and browser identity/onboarding; existing declared-client/UI stage5 functional work retained; explicit policy/bootstrap and cleanup read integration. Do not duplicate those requests or require completed unrelated stages before this package can develop. Highest implementation priority remains test-overhead ecbc722a, followed by acts and builder-identified Jam blockers; this request adds no first-Jam readiness gate. Report source/design discrepancies before weakening scope.","priority":"After highest-priority test-overhead ecbc722a; preserve acts/Jam-blocker/Jam-and-docs order. No new first-Jam gate.","target_head":"e6e6782830e0ca8a68f0d11c4d4ece5e4e98c967","target_ref":"refs/heads/main","target_repo":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3","to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}